        of ``{NAME: bool}``, booleans ONLY.

        Lets the config UI mask an api_key / base_url (and an MCP server's auth
        token / stdio env-vars) that's already set in .env (or the process env)
        with a placeholder, without ever reading the value back. Strictly
        write-only: this returns neither secrets NOR URLs, only whether each NAME
        has a non-empty value. Keys and base URLs are treated identically — no
        value of any kind leaves the server here.
        """
